Source: ps3-splash
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), librsvg2-bin
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ps3-splash
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, plymouth, plymouth-label, fonts-dejavu-core
# Plymouth depends on initramfs-tools | dracut only to put itself into an initramfs; the PS3 boots
# without one (Petitboot loads /boot/vmlinux-<release> directly), and initramfs-tools would build
# an unused initramfs on every kernel install (minutes on the PS3)
Provides: initramfs-tools
Description: Walnut Linux boot splash (Plymouth theme)
 The Walnut Linux logo on the desktop's blue with a text progress bar (a walnut rolling at
 its head) and status jokes, for boot and shutdown. Kernels whose arguments include
 "splash" show it; the others show the usual boot messages.
